    "lawCode": "Amd §41, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5632\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nimplementing a provision in a collective bargaining agreement between\nthe state university construction fund and an employee organization\nrelating to unused sick leave and retirement service credit\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nImplements a provision from a collective bargaining agreement between\nSUNY construction fund and its employees\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n§ 1 - amends section 41j of the Retirement and Social Security Law to\npermit employees of the State University Construction Fund to use up\nto two hundred days of accumulated unused sick leave for retirement\nservice credit.\n\n§2 - provides that all past service costs shall be borne by the SUNY\nconstruction fund and may be amortized over a five year period.\n\n§3 - provides for an effective date April 1, 2003 to implement a\nprovision in the collective bargaining agreement between the State\nUniversity Construction Fund and the CSEA local that represents the\nFund's bargaining unit employees.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nCurrently, the maximum is 165 days for these covered employees.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nUnder section 41(j)(1) of the Retirement and Social Security Law, a\nmember of a public retirement system may, upon retirement, receive an\nadditional day's pension credit for each day of accumulated unused\nsick leave, to a maximum of 165 days.\n\nUnder chapters 103, part A and 419 of the laws of 2004, executive\nbranch M/C employees or an employee in a position listed in the\nvarious state negotiating units may use up to 200 days of accumulated\nunused sick leave for a pension credit. These chapters of the Laws of\n2004 were enacted to implement the collective bargaining agreements\nthat the State reached with its unions for the agreements which\ncovered the period April 1, 2003 through March 31, 2007. The State\nUniversity Construction Fund entered into a collective bargaining\nagreement with its bargaining unit employees for the same period of\ntime which also permitted its employees to use up to a maximum of 200\ndays of accumulated unused sick leave for retirement service credit.\nThrough oversight, the Fund was not included in the legislation that\namended section 410)(1) of the Retirement and Social Security Law to\nimplement the change that was agreed to in the collective bargaining\nagreements.\n\nIn 2005, the Legislature again amended section 410)(1) of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law to include employees of the\nDormitory Authority, the Thruway Authority and the Canal Corporation\nin order to implement the ability to use up to a maximum of 200 such\ndays for pension credit that is contained in their collective\nbargaining agreements. This bill would put Fund employees, in regard\nto the maximum number of sick days that can be used for retirement\nservice credit, on par with State and some public authority employees.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2008 Session: A.11627/S.8577 - passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nIf this bill is enacted, there will be a total past service cost of\napproximately $21,300 which would be borne by the New York State\nUniversity Construction Fund. If this cost is amortized over a period\nof 5 years, the cost for the first year, including interest, would be\napproximately $4,940. In addition to the past service cost, there\ncould be future increases in the annual contributions of the New York\nState University Construction Fund.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nRetroactively to April 1, 2003 to implement the provision contained in\nthe collective bargaining agreement.\n",
